{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["Oil for the lamp. All matters of this pericah concern the fittings of the structure, for it is not the way of a king to come to his house until it is fitted with light, and from that same oil itself they shall take for the needs of the anointing, to consecrate with it the entire structure." "<b>Fragrances.</b> Mixed into the anointing oil. It is the way of kings to fragrance the house for themselves before they enter it." "<b>And for the incense of spices.</b> Divide it: and the spices — for the incense. And one should not say fragrances are for the needs of the incense of spices, for in the entire making of the incense there were no fragrances at all, but only spices, and the verses prove this in pericat Tissa."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:00:18.771632636Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}